language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ bin_packing: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Given several items of specific weights and a number of bins of a fixed capacity, assign each item to a bin so that the total weight of the items in each bin does not exceed the capacity.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `bin_packing.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/bin_packing.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `bin_packing_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py bin_packing.json
$   savilerow model.eprime bin_packing_1.param -run-solver

$ number of items, derived from the data: the length of weights (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given weights_dim1 : int
letting n = weights_dim1
$ weights[i]: weight of item i (indices 1-based, so the data's index 0 is weights[1])
given weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int
$ capacity of each bin
given capacity : int
$ number of bins available, numbered 0 to num_bins-1
given num_bins : int
letting last = num_bins - 1
$ bins[i]: bin that item i is assigned to, 0-indexed as in the problem (the output, indices 1-based)
$ a single value per item, so each item lies in exactly one bin
find bins : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..last)

branching on [bins]
such that
$ the total weight of the items assigned to each bin does not exceed the capacity of the bin
forAll b : int(0..last) . (sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(bins[i] = b) * weights[i]) <= capacity
